CHANGELOG
=========

0.12.1: 2026-11-09
-------------------

Bug fixes (Round 7 upstream triage, findings 116–123, all closed):

Vim semantics & key bindings:

- Added ``ZZ`` (write + quit) and ``ZQ`` (quit without saving) navigation-mode
  bindings (finding 116).
- ``Ctrl-[`` now leaves insert mode like ``Esc`` (finding 119); a numeric prefix
  before ``i``/``a`` repeats the typed text on exit, e.g. ``5itest<Esc>`` inserts
  five copies (finding 120).
- ``>>`` / ``<<`` now indent by ``tabstop``/``expandtab`` with undo support
  instead of a hardcoded width (finding 118).
- ``*`` / ``#`` record the word in search history, so ``/<Up>`` recalls it and
  bare ``:s`` reuses it (finding 122).

Commands & I/O:

- ``:w!`` force-writes read-only files (granting owner-write for one write,
  then restoring the mode); ``:wqa!`` now forwards ``force`` to each buffer
  write (finding 117).
- ``:s`` rejects nested-quantifier patterns (e.g. ``(a+)+$``) with an
  ``Unsafe pattern`` message instead of freezing on catastrophic backtracking
  (finding 123).

Highlighting:

- Extensionless files are highlighted via content sniffing (a python shebang
  pins ``PythonLexer``, otherwise ``guess_lexer`` on a 4 KiB sample), cached
  per location on both lexer branches (finding 121).

- Full test suite passing: 274 passed, mypy clean on 57 source files, ruff clean.

0.12.0: 2026-11-09
-------------------

Packaging, Thai package & modernization (since 0.11.2):

- Reorganized flat ``thai*.py`` modules into the ``vith.thai`` package
  (``classify.py``, ``clusters.py``, ``words.py``, ``patches.py``) with a lazy
  ``vith.thai_*`` compat layer and full backward compatibility.
- Adopted Python 3.10 idioms: PEP 585 built-in generics, ``str.removeprefix``,
  ``itertools.pairwise`` / ``yield from``, and ``match``/``case`` dispatch.
- Round 6 deep audit (findings 110–115, 76 items, all closed): wrong-logic fixes
  (substitute identical match, ``:wqa!``, empty-command no-op, pyflakes syntax
  errors, UTF-8 columns, cold-text undo/reset, ``HttpIO.exists``, encoding
  restore, Thai renderer guards); ``None``/bounds hardening; dead-code and
  duplication sweeps (unified splits, shared pager/lexer helpers); bounded
  caches and fast paths (lexer LRU, cell-starts guard, SARA-AM single pass);
  readability pass (nonlocal flag, explicit ``None``, PathLike/UTF-8 rc-file,
  ``EOFError``/``KeyboardInterrupt`` pager guard, byte-slice process title).
- Follow-up hardening: exotic-mapping escape fallback, desync-tolerant
  ``close_buffer``, documented compat retention.
- Full test suite passing: 250 passed, mypy clean on 57 source files, ruff clean.

0.11.2: 2026-11-09
-------------------

Bug fixes & robustness (Round 5 audit arc, 17 findings 093–109):

Vim semantics & commands:

- Fixed ``:set ic`` / ``:set ignorecase`` preview leak where aborting preview (``Esc``)
  silently kept case-insensitivity active for the remainder of the session (finding 093).
- Added support for ``:s`` flags ``i`` (ignorecase) and ``I`` (noignorecase); rejected invalid
  flags with Vim ``E488: Trailing characters`` (finding 094).
- In multi-window/multi-tab layouts, ``:q`` now checks for unsaved changes only in the
  active window's buffer instead of being blocked by dirty buffers in other windows (finding 095).
- ``:e <location>`` now checks for unsaved changes and honors ``!`` (``force``) before
  switching buffers (finding 096).
- Canonicalized untitled buffer name across status bar, ``:ls``, and buffers overlay
  to ``[New file]`` (``UNTITLED_LABEL``) (finding 107).
- Command line mutual-exclusion flags (``-p``, ``-o``, ``-O``) raise ``ValueError`` defensively
  inside ``load_initial_files`` instead of a bare assert (finding 107).

Thai & Lao script support & renderer:

- Reorganized flat ``thai*.py`` files (``thai.py``, ``thai_classify.py``, ``thai_clusters.py``,
  ``thai_words.py``) into a dedicated ``vith.thai`` package (``classify.py``, ``clusters.py``,
  ``words.py``, ``patches.py``) with full backward compatibility.
- Sticky Thai renderer gate is now latched on multi-line paste, undo/redo, and full-text
  assignments when Thai text is introduced on non-cursor rows (finding 097).
- Re-entrant differential renderer calls now reliably restore ``screen.zero_width_escapes``
  under an outer ``try/finally`` block (finding 098).
- Hoisted Thai cluster calculation imports in ``ColdTextBuffer._cursor_vertical`` to module
  level, eliminating per-keystroke import overhead on ``j``/``k`` (finding 102).
- Added ``_cell_has_sara_am`` fast-path check in ``_sanitize_and_invalidate_sara_am`` to skip
  key sorting and set allocations on rows without SARA AM (finding 109).

Performance, storage & completion:

- Rewrote ``BufferListOverlay.highlight_location`` to produce chunked token spans rather than
  per-character fragments and loops (finding 109).
- Expanded ``DocumentWordsCompleter`` cache key with ``line_start`` to detect text shifts on lines
  prior to the cursor line (finding 109).
- Preserved original trailing newline status across buffer save and reload (``EditorBuffer.write``),
  ensuring files without an ending newline do not acquire one unconditionally (finding 103).
- Fixed ``_LazyStylesDict`` containment: ``__getitem__`` raises ``KeyError`` on unknown styles so that
  standard ``Mapping.__contains__`` (``'style' in editor.styles``) returns ``False`` instead of raising
  ``ClassNotFound`` (finding 103).
- Fixed example ``vithrc`` F9 execution callback to guard against ``None`` buffer and abort on write
  failures (finding 103).

Testing, tooling & packaging:

- ``tools/bench_quez_cold_text.py`` benchmarks shipped ``vith.cold_text.ColdTextStack`` instead of a
  private duplicate, with corrected ``measure_ms`` naming and fixture truncation (finding 099).
- Refreshed reproducible benchmark figures in ``docs/speed_latency_plan.md`` (finding 100).
- Repaired vacuous/flaky assertions in tests, replaced inspect-based tests with functional execution,
  and cleaned up unused mock assignments (finding 101).
- Updated packaging and documentation floors: prompt_toolkit ``>=3.0.0,<3.1.0``, cleaned dead
  ``setup.py`` and ``requirements-dev.txt`` references, added tool cache directories to ``.gitignore``
  (finding 104).
- Cleaned up build/dist release artifacts from source tree (finding 105).
- Dead code cleanup across decorators, previewers, classifier sets, and cold-text metadata (finding 106).
- Type-annotated ``current_editor_buffer -> EditorBuffer | None`` with explicit ``return None`` and
  corrected ``is_thai_base`` docstring (finding 108).
- Full test suite passing: 217 passed, 1 skipped, mypy clean on 56 source files, ruff clean.

0.11.1: 2026-11-09
-------------------

Bug fixes:

Thai & Lao script support:

- Visual-block selection (``<C-v>``) on lines containing SARA AM (``U+0E33``) or
  fewer combining marks than corner rows no longer overshoots mid-line:
  ``_thai_selection_range_at_line`` and ``_thai_selection_ranges`` clamp
  selection bounds strictly to cell-cluster boundaries within line margins
  instead of unconditionally bleeding ``prompt_toolkit`` codepoint columns
  (finding 092).

Documentation & audit:

- OKF v0.2 documentation bundle synchronized to 92 machine-verified findings:
  cataloged finding 092, resolved missing Round 3 Addendum table in
  ``docs/bugs/index.md``, and synchronized update logs.

0.11.0: 2026-11-08
-------------------

Field-verified correctness arcs since 0.10.0 (documented in detail in
``docs/bugs/index.md``: 91 machine-verified findings, all closed; every fix
carries regression tests):

Thai & Lao script support:

- Visual-mode correctness: visual selections, visual blocks and block
  ``I``/``A`` insert positions align on **cell-cluster columns** — Thai/Lao
  clusters highlight, cut, yank and insert like Vim cells (findings 076-085).
- ``j``/``k`` keep the *visual* column across Thai rows (``preferred_column``
  was a raw codepoint column; finding 078).
- Word spans no longer slice mixed-script clusters (Latin base + Thai mark,
  generic accents) for ``iw``/``aw``/``*``/``#`` (finding 086).
- Cluster-safe counted operations: counted ``$`` (``3$``), line-local
  ``e``/``E`` snapping, whole-cell ``2rX``, counted ``~`` respecting
  ``:set tildeop`` (findings 053, 063, 071).
- ``:s`` with a Thai replacement re-arms the SARA-AM neighbor sanitizer; gate
  latching/decay covers Thai file names and message banners
  (findings 081, 082).

Editor commands & buffers:

- ``:b`` fixes: untitled-buffer crash (080), completed patterns jumping, a
  1-based numbering shared by ``:b <n>``/``:ls``/``BufferListOverlay`` and
  ``[New file]`` names (findings 067, 080, 087).
- ``:s`` flags parsing (``:s/x/y//g``, ``gg``, multi-letter flags) with
  ``:0,1s/`` mapping to the first line (finding 083).
- ``:e`` on a file deleted since it was read shows E211-style error and keeps
  the in-memory contents (finding 088).
- ``:q``/``:wqa`` window-vs-exit semantics; ``:bd`` across tabs keeps the
  invariant (findings 066, 067, 070).
- ``__main__`` import guard, reporter invalidation, aborted ``:set`` preview
  leak fix (``:set paste`` × ``Esc``), I/O robustness (latin-1 → utf-8 save
  fallback, unknown-backend read-only buffers), first-run startup fixes
  (findings 068, 069, 091, 070).

Performance & maintenance:

- Thai ``j``/``k`` cell-start scans cached with LRU (~762 µs per keypress on
  2000-codepoint rows → O(1)); megabyte line span-cache bypass; lazy-import
  hoists in the cursor path; ``:s`` single-split reuse (finding 090).
- ``thai.py`` split into ``thai_classify``/``thai_clusters``/``thai_words``;
  the prompt_toolkit patch installer moved out of import time into
  ``Editor.__init__`` (finding 075).
- Dead-code sweep including a working ``.vithrc`` example; duplicate ``:set``
  logic consolidated into a single catalog; duplicate word-walk logic unified
  into one generator (findings 073, 074).

0.10.0: 2026-11-08
------------------

Cold text:

- Compressed undo/redo history via ``quez``: snapshots are stored compressed
  with Zstandard level 1 by default. Configure with
  ``editor.cold_text_compression`` in ``.vithrc`` (``zstd``, ``zlib``,
  ``zlib-fast``, ``zlib-best``, ``lzo`` or ``none``). Inspect current buffer
  statistics with ``:compression``.
- Added the ``lzo`` optional dependency extra.

0.9.1: 2026-11-08
-----------------

Packaging:

- Fix PyPI author credits metadata rendering in pyproject.toml (PEP 621).

0.9.0: 2026-11-08
-----------------

Forking and rebranding to Vith (Vi + Thai support)

- Renamed project from pyvim to vith: PEP 621 packaging
  (setup.py → pyproject.toml), Python 3.10+ requirement, console script `vith`,
  README.md with fork attribution; BSD 3-clause license retained with stacked
  copyright (© 2015-2023 Jonathan Slenders, © 2026 Chaiwat Suttipongsakul);
  upstream repository linked to https://github.com/prompt-toolkit/pyvim;
  original PyVim changelog preserved verbatim below as historical appendix.

Stability, performance and international input:

- Fixed the Python 3.14+/3.15 ``asyncio.get_event_loop()`` startup crash:
  opening any file before the event loop runs no longer aborts ``vith``.
- Added Thai & Lao script support: terminal cell-cluster navigation and
  edits (``h``, ``l``, ``j``, ``k``, ``x``, ``X``, ``s``, ``r``, ``~``, ``$``,
  ``e``...), two-tier Thai word segmentation (libthai, with an
  orthographic fallback), and SARA AM (U+0E33/U+0EB3) differential renderer
  fixes. See ``docs/thai_support_plan.md``.
- Latency work (``docs/speed_latency_plan.md``): streaming + cached
  Pygments highlighting, per-line word-span caching for Thai word
  motions, lazy colorscheme loading, singleton word completion cache and
  an O(1) pyflakes error index.

Bug fixes (machine-verified findings bundle, ``docs/bugs/``):

- ``:s`` with a line range beyond EOF reports ``E19`` instead of crashing;
  the cursor lands on the last substituted line.
- jedi is optional: ``.py`` completion falls back to word completion when
  jedi is not installed instead of crashing.
- A failed ``:w`` no longer terminates the editor through ``:wq``/``:wqa``;
  unknown locations report an error without side effects.
- ReportingProcessor runs before tab expansion so pyflakes error columns
  stay aligned on tab-indented lines, and the message toolbar shows all
  errors of the cursor line.
- Buffer numbering inserts new buffers after the active one; command
  grammar alternation is deterministic.

Tooling and packaging:

- Added ruff (lint + format) and a mypy baseline checked against the
  packaging floor; ``tox`` setup replaced by ``pyproject.toml [project.optional-dependencies] dev``.
- Python floor is now ``python_requires='>=3.10'``; prompt_toolkit floor
  raised to 3.0; ``six`` and the python 2 directives removed.


